proof.text:
For an arbitrary natural transformation $\eta:F\Rightarrow G$, the two upper-sign morphisms in the asserted square satisfy
$$\iota^m_{GK}\alpha^-_{G,K}\eta_{\tau^{\le m}K}
=G(\iota^m_K)\eta_{\tau^{\le m}K}
=\eta_K F(\iota^m_K)
=\iota^m_{GK}\tau^{\le m}(\eta_K)\alpha^-_{F,K}.$$
Naturality of $\eta$ gives the middle equality; naturality of $\iota^m$ gives the last. Since $F\tau^{\le m}K\in\mathcal D^{\le m}$, step 1's injectivity gives the upper-sign compatibility. No shift compatibility of $\eta$ is used.
